Enhancement: Resume interrupted backups without re-reading files

When a backup was interrupted, the next run had to read all files again that
were new or changed compared to the parent snapshot, even if they had already
been uploaded. For large backups this could take hours or days.

Restic now keeps an encrypted journal of the directories completed during a
backup in its local cache. If the backup is interrupted, the next backup of
the same paths from the same host no longer reads the unchanged files in
these directories. The journal is removed once a backup completes. Resuming
requires the cache and is not used together with `--force` or `--dry-run`.

